  <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="d_2026-01-01_2026-06-30" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerTextBlock" id="c3246274" escape="true">
   <p style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><b><em style="font: inherit;">7.</em> Revenue and Accounts Receivable</b> </p>
   <p style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><span style="background-color:#ffffff;"><i><b>California Ethanol Revenues: </b></i></span>We sell our ethanol segment products to J.D. Heiskell, which sells them to <em style="font: inherit;">third</em> parties designated by us. We record revenue for ethanol when we transfer ethanol into our storage tank, which is leased to J.D. Heiskell, and when product is loaded into shipping trucks for products other than ethanol.&#160;We also buy our corn feedstock from J.D. Heiskell. Transaction prices for ethanol sales and corn purchases are based on daily market prices. We invoice J.D. Heiskell each business day for the net balance between ethanol and other product sales and our corn purchases, and J.D. Heiskell pays on the next business day. In the <em style="font: inherit;">first</em> <em style="font: inherit;">six</em> months of&#160;<span style="background-color:#fff;"><em style="font: inherit;">2026</em></span>, we recognized Section <em style="font: inherit;">45Z</em> PTC income&#160;upon production of eligible ethanol. The following table lists the California Ethanol segment revenues:</p>
   <p style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
